Actually I tend to stay away from advancing the secondary weapon skill
(unless of course it's dagger, for the other reasons Janis stated).
The chance to hit is determined by the lesser of the primary weapon
skill and the two-weaponing skill. The reason it's so crappy in the
beginning of the game is your level and stats can't yet overcome the
penalties to hit. I usually follow this path, at least with samurai.
Adapt as necessary for other classes: 1) advance long sword to Expert.
2) Once it's there, use the first co-aligned altar (barring an early
wish extravaganza) to get Snickersnee, slide the katana to the second
hand, and #twoweapon. 3) replace snickersnee (preferably with a
foobrand).

I wouldn't bother with the Tsurugi unless I hadn't yet found a
secondary weapon worth using. It's decent in the midgame, but a waste
of skill slots, especially if you plan on using daggers or the yumi,
and it stinks later on.


